      {
        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "6327d9d3-e72a-5cd6-8e45-f1822aa21ac1",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Gaetano Donizetti, Vincenzo Bellini, Felice Romani, Charles Nodier, Isidore Justin Séverin Taylor, Eugenio Cavallini, Saverio Mercadante, Giuseppe Verdi, Federico Ricci, Domenico Ronzani, Domenico Gilardoni\n- Works: Lucrezia Borgia, Il pirata, Bertram, ou le Pirate, Raimonde, Gemma di Vergy, Maria Stuarda, Il giuramento, Il bravo, Oberto, Un giorno di regno, Maria Padilla, Nabucco, I Lombardi alla prima crociata, Giovanna d'Arco, Estella di Murcia, Salvator Rosa, I pazzi per progetto\n- Organizations: La Scala\n- Concepts: opera, melodramatic opera, farce, libretto, world premiere\n\nFacts:\n- In 1826, Charles Nodier and Isidore Justin Séverin Taylor created the three-act mélodrame Bertram, ou le Pirate and Raimonde, which later served as the basis for Il pirata.\n- Lucrezia Borgia is a melodramatic opera in a prologue and two acts by Gaetano Donizetti.\n- In 1833, Eugenio Cavallini conducted the world premiere of Gaetano Donizetti's Lucrezia Borgia at La Scala.\n- In 1834, Eugenio Cavallini conducted the world premiere of Gaetano Donizetti's Gemma di Vergy at La Scala.\n- In 1835, Eugenio Cavallini conducted the world premiere of Gaetano Donizetti's Maria Stuarda at La Scala.\n- In 1837, Eugenio Cavallini conducted the world premiere of Saverio Mercadante's Il giuramento at La Scala.\n- In 1839, Eugenio Cavallini conducted the world premieres of Saverio Mercadante's Il bravo and Giuseppe Verdi's Oberto at La Scala.\n- In 1840, Eugenio Cavallini conducted the world premiere of Giuseppe Verdi's Un giorno di regno at La Scala.\n- In 1841, Eugenio Cavallini conducted the world premiere of Gaetano Donizetti's Maria Padilla at La Scala.\n- In 1842, Eugenio Cavallini conducted the world premiere of Giuseppe Verdi's Nabucco at La Scala.\n- In 1843, Eugenio Cavallini conducted the world premiere of Giuseppe Verdi's I Lombardi alla prima crociata at La Scala.\n- In 1845, Eugenio Cavallini conducted the world premiere of Giuseppe Verdi's Giovanna d'Arco at La Scala.\n- In 1846, Eugenio Cavallini conducted the world premiere of Federico Ricci's Estella di Murcia at La Scala.\n- In 1854, Eugenio Cavallini conducted the world premiere of Domenico Ronzani's Salvator Rosa at La Scala.\n- Il pirata is an opera in two acts by Vincenzo Bellini with an Italian libretto by Felice Romani.\n- I pazzi per progetto is a one-act farce by Gaetano Donizetti with a libretto by Domenico Gilardoni.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "aaf2bc01-c563-5366-8976-58bfbac5c683",
        "text": "Page: Lucrezia Borgia (opera). Sentence: Lucrezia Borgia is a melodramatic opera in a prologue and two acts by Gaetano Donizetti.\nPage: Il pirata. Sentence: Il pirata (\"The Pirate\") is an opera in two acts by Vincenzo Bellini to an Italian libretto by Felice Romani which was based on a three-act mélodrame from 1826, \"Bertram, ou le Pirate\" (\"Bertram, or The Pirate\") by Charles Nodier and \"Raimonde\" (actually Isidore Justin Séverin Taylor).\nPage: Eugenio Cavallini. Sentence: He also served as a conductor at La Scala, notably leading the world premieres of Gaetano Donizetti's \"Lucrezia Borgia\" (1833), Donizetti's \"Gemma di Vergy\" (1834), Donizetti's \"Maria Stuarda\" (1835), Saverio Mercadante's \"Il giuramento\" (1837), Mercadante's \"Il bravo\" (1839), Giuseppe Verdi's \"Oberto\" (1839), Verdi's \"Un giorno di regno\" (1840), Donizetti's \"Maria Padilla\" (1841), Verdi's \"Nabucco\" (1842), Verdi's \"I Lombardi alla prima crociata\" (1843), Verdi's \"Giovanna d'Arco\" (1845), Federico Ricci's \"Estella di Murcia\" (1846), and Domenico Ronzani's \"Salvator Rosa\" (1854).\nPage: I pazzi per progetto. Sentence: I Pazzi per progetto (\"Madmen by Design\") is a farce in one act by Gaetano Donizetti to a libretto by Domenico Gilardoni.",
        "type": "DocumentChunk"
